WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.372
It was Christmas Eve.

2
00:00:04.373 --> 00:00:10.802
Speedy and Boomer were about to start their new job.

3
00:00:10.803 --> 00:00:15.036
The two reindeer looked around the warehouse.

4
00:00:15.037 --> 00:00:20.623
They saw a huge, pretty sleigh.

5
00:00:20.624 --> 00:00:24.639
Colorful presents filled tall shelves.

6
00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:28.651
Elves scurried around everywhere.

7
00:00:28.652 --> 00:00:32.169
"Hey there!" said a friendly voice.

8
00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:34.473
Speedy and Boomer turned around.

9
00:00:34.474 --> 00:00:39.380
"I'm Rudolph," said a reindeer with a shiny red nose.

10
00:00:39.381 --> 00:00:42.604
"I'm the reindeer in charge.

11
00:00:42.605 --> 00:00:47.803
Our job tonight is to pull that sleigh through the air."

12
00:00:47.804 --> 00:00:51.353
"That sounds easy," said Boomer.

13
00:00:51.354 --> 00:00:53.985
Rudolph nodded. "It's not hard.

14
00:00:53.986 --> 00:00:59.019
But our boss, Santa, has lots of stops to make.

15
00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:04.073
We'll stop at millions of houses all over the world."

16
00:01:04.074 --> 00:01:11.739
"Whoa!" Speedy gasped. "One night isn't enough time!"

17
00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:14.343
"Don't worry," said Rudolph.

18
00:01:14.344 --> 00:01:18.209
"We will have 24 hours of night."

19
00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:30.884
"Huh?" said Boomer. "How is that possible?"

20
00:01:30.885 --> 00:01:38.289
Rudolph led Boomer and Speedy to a giant map.

21
00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:44.274
"Earth is divided into 24 time zones," said Rudolph.

22
00:01:44.275 --> 00:01:49.938
"Because there are 24 hours in one day?" asked Speedy.

23
00:01:49.939 --> 00:01:52.572
"Right," said Rudolph.

24
00:01:52.573 --> 00:01:57.258
"The sun only shines on one side of Earth at a time.

25
00:01:57.259 --> 00:02:03.066
So it's always daytime in some places and nighttime in others."

26
00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:05.433
"Let me show you."

27
00:02:05.434 --> 00:02:07.591
Rudolph pressed a button.

28
00:02:07.592 --> 00:02:12.375
A big part of the map went dark.

29
00:02:12.376 --> 00:02:20.864
"When it's 11:00 p.m. in Japan, it's only 11:00 a.m. in Argentina," Rudolph said.

30
00:02:20.865 --> 00:02:26.909
"Argentina's time is 12 hours behind Japan's."

31
00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:30.363
He pressed another button.

32
00:02:30.364 --> 00:02:32.853
A zigzag line appeared.

33
00:02:32.854 --> 00:02:37.062
"This is the International Date Line," said Rudolph.

34
00:02:37.063 --> 00:02:39.795
"Each day starts here.

35
00:02:39.796 --> 00:02:47.741
We'll start at this line and fly west."

36
00:02:47.742 --> 00:02:52.717
"How long will we spend in each time zone?" asked Speedy.

37
00:02:52.718 --> 00:02:58.972
"One hour. Then we'll move west to the next time zone," said Rudolph.

38
00:02:58.973 --> 00:03:05.122
"Oh! The time will be one hour earlier there!" said Boomer.

39
00:03:05.123 --> 00:03:08.133
"Exactly!" said Rudolph.

40
00:03:08.134 --> 00:03:09.567
"We should get ready.

41
00:03:09.568 --> 00:03:13.233
We have 24 time zones to visit!"

42
00:03:13.234 --> 00:03:16.537
"That's a lot of flying," said Boomer.

43
00:03:16.538 --> 00:03:19.185
"I'm going to get hungry."

44
00:03:19.186 --> 00:03:23.473
"Many children leave treats for us," said Rudolph.

45
00:03:23.474 --> 00:03:33.089
"But watch out—the boss usually eats them all!"

